<% page_title "Privacy policy" %>
<% meta description: "How DeNshe Jewellery collects and looks after your personal information when you shop with us." %>

<header class="page-intro">
  <div class="page page--narrow">
    <p class="eyebrow">DeNshe Jewellery</p>
    <h1>Privacy policy.</h1>
    <p class="lede">A plain note on what we collect, why we ask for it, and how we keep it. Last updated <%= Date.current.strftime("%-d %B %Y") %>.</p>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="section section--tight">
  <div class="page page--narrow prose">
    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>DeNshe Jewellery (“DeNshe”, “we”, “us”) is a jewellery label based in Anand, Gujarat, India. You can reach us at <%= mail_to brand.email %>.</p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>When you place an order or write to us, we may collect your name, phone number, email address, shipping and billing address, and the details of what you ordered. Payment card or UPI details are handled by our payment partner and are not stored on our servers.</p>

    <h2>How we use it</h2>
    <p>We use your information to fulfil orders, answer questions, improve the DeNshe Jewellery shop, and meet legal or accounting duties. We do not sell your information.</p>

    <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
    <p>We share only what is needed with trusted partners — for example, payment processing and delivery. They may process your information only to provide that service for DeNshe Jewellery.</p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>We keep order and contact records for as long as we need them for the shop, support, and the law. You can ask us what we hold about you, or to update or delete it, by writing to <%= mail_to brand.email %>.</p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>Our site uses cookies and similar storage so your cart, session, and preferences work. We may also use Google Analytics to understand how people visit denshe.shop. You can control cookies in your browser; some shopping features need them to function.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy as the shop grows. The date at the top will change when we do. Continuing to use denshe.shop after an update means you accept the revised policy.</p>
  </div>
</section>
